From 9c6eb36c4eafacc0e05402d49fa7134a83f52e1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: booomxd <122612016+booomxd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 03:08:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fuzz the parsers inside cargo test; a damaged shader operand
 no longer panics

The parsers read bytes nobody vouches for: the user's dump, its import
libraries, its shader containers and their programs. A malformed field
must be an error, never a panic. victory-core gains `fuzz`: a seeded
mutator (edge values on known fields, nudges, cuts, copied runs,
appended bytes) that runs each target on 4,096 damaged cases of an
input the test builds itself, so no game data is read and CI runs it
as it is. A failure names its target, seed and case.

Targets: PE32+ images (one synthetic image with imports, delay
imports, an export, TLS callbacks and a CodeView record), COFF import
libraries, shader containers down to the native programs and their
decoding, and every stage of the translation of a compute program
(spill, structure, resources, I/O, emit). VICTORY_FUZZ_CASES and
VICTORY_FUZZ_SEED let a developer search longer.

The translation target found one panic: the search for parked scalars
in ir.rs kept a flag per scalar code below 128 and indexed it with any
code an operand named, so a damaged word naming code 255 was an index
out of bounds that took the run down. The flags now cover all 256
codes; the case is kept as a regression test. 30 million more cases
of each target found nothing else.
